macOS: keep window contents in step with the window during a live resize

Target: SDL release-3.4.14     Apply with: git apply <this file>

Two things make the contents judder and lag behind the window edge while it is
dragged, both fixed here:

1. METAL_RenderPresent presents fire-and-forget, so a frame can reach the screen
   a refresh or two late, by which time the window is a different size. Enables
   CAMetalLayer.presentsWithTransaction while inLiveResize and presents once the
   command buffer is scheduled, so the frame joins the CATransaction the resize
   is committed under. Outside a drag the original path is unchanged.

2. Between presented frames AppKit scales the layer's contents to the view's new
   bounds. windowDidResize: now pins them to the corner opposite the dragged
   edge, taken from the window's frame delta (the pointer sits on the window
   border during a drag and cannot identify the edge reliably). Applied to the
   Metal view's layer-backed ancestors too, only when the corner changes, and a
   no-op for non-Metal windows.

Addresses https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/issues/12081 , unfixed as of 3.4.14.
Measured on Stella (github.com/stella-emu/stella): each half was removed in turn
from the working build and the artifacts returned.

diff --git a/src/render/metal/SDL_render_metal.m b/src/render/metal/SDL_render_metal.m
index 989809c..aa31df3 100644
--- a/src/render/metal/SDL_render_metal.m
+++ b/src/render/metal/SDL_render_metal.m
@@ -2013,6 +2013,19 @@ static bool METAL_RenderPresent(SDL_Renderer *renderer)
     @autoreleasepool {
         SDL3METAL_RenderData *data = (__bridge SDL3METAL_RenderData *)renderer->internal;
         bool ready = true;
+        BOOL syncpresent = NO;
+
+#if defined(SDL_PLATFORM_MACOS) && defined(SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_COCOA)
+        /* During a drag, tie the drawable to the CATransaction the resize is
+         * committed under, so the frame and the new window bounds land
+         * together. Costs a CPU wait, so only while inLiveResize. */
+        if (data.mtlview) {
+            syncpresent = ((__bridge NSView *)data.mtlview).inLiveResize;
+        }
+        if (data.mtllayer.presentsWithTransaction != syncpresent) {
+            data.mtllayer.presentsWithTransaction = syncpresent;
+        }
+#endif
 
         // If we don't have a command buffer, we can't present, so activate to get one.
         if (data.mtlcmdencoder == nil) {
@@ -2032,11 +2045,20 @@ static bool METAL_RenderPresent(SDL_Renderer *renderer)
         //  But we'll still try to commit the command buffer in case it was already enqueued.
         if (ready) {
             SDL_assert(data.mtlbackbuffer != nil);
-            [data.mtlcmdbuffer presentDrawable:data.mtlbackbuffer];
+            // presentsWithTransaction presents by hand instead; see below
+            if (!syncpresent) {
+                [data.mtlcmdbuffer presentDrawable:data.mtlbackbuffer];
+            }
         }
 
         [data.mtlcmdbuffer commit];
 
+        if (syncpresent && ready) {
+            // Scheduled, not completed: enough to join the transaction
+            [data.mtlcmdbuffer waitUntilScheduled];
+            [data.mtlbackbuffer present];
+        }
+
         data.mtlcmdencoder = nil;
         data.mtlcmdbuffer = nil;
         data.mtlbackbuffer = nil;
